# Task routing

Before specialized investigation or edits, classify the requested outcome using the generated skill
index in `AGENTS.md`. Read the matching skill and its linked role before doing that work. Select by
intent, not only file extension. State the selected workflow and role briefly in the first update.

- Harness review or changes (instruction loading, rules, roles, skills, agent checks): use
  `ai/skills/maintain-agent-harness/SKILL.md`.
- Product code or architecture review without implementation: use `ai/skills/review-change/SKILL.md`.
- Backend implementation, debugging, refactoring, configuration, persistence, or migrations: use
  `ai/skills/implement-service-slice/SKILL.md`.

An explicitly requested role takes precedence; still load the workflow matching the task. For a mixed
task, load each workflow when entering its phase rather than loading every role in advance. A request
for review alone does not authorize implementation. Re-evaluate routing if the scope changes.

For a task outside these triggers, follow core rules and explain the relevant approach; do not force
an unrelated skill or create a new role just to cover a one-off task. Ask only when ambiguity affects
the requested outcome. Scoped rules apply by both matching paths and relevant behavior, including
work outside their globs that changes the same safety boundary.
